# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GUARD RAILS. These patterns block the files that still contain participants'
# real names. Do not remove them.
#
# Git history is permanent: if any of these is committed even once, deleting it
# in a later commit does NOT remove it from the repository, and on a public
# repo it may already have been cloned, forked or indexed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The ID -> real name mapping. This is the re-identification key.
participants.csv
**/participants.csv

# Raw collection tree: the per-session directory names embed participants'
# real names, e.g. "33004-42675 - FIRSTNAME SURNAME - 22 November, 2020".
Data/
**/Data/

# Un-pseudonymised parsed CSVs: these still carry a participant_name column.
Output/
**/Output/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Large regenerable intermediates (~1.5 GB), well over GitHub's limits
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.parquet
*.pkl
Result/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# LaTeX build artefacts
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.log
*.out
*.synctex.gz
